CAT = "dronPlan"; SEG = "PLN"
Q = [
("Which chart shows the boundaries of permanent controlled and special use airspace for planning a drone flight?",
 "A visual navigation chart", ["A topographic tramping map", "A road atlas", "A council zoning map"],
 "AC101-1 says Visual Navigation Charts show the boundaries of permanent uncontrolled, controlled and special use airspace, and can be bought from the Aeronautical Information Shop."),
("Which VNC series is best suited to low-level local flying?",
 "The C series at 1:250,000", ["The B series at 1:500,000", "A world chart at 1:1,000,000", "A road map at 1:50,000"],
 "The CAA airspace guide says the C1 to C14 charts at 1:250,000 cover the whole country and suit low level and local navigation."),
("Where can a drone pilot view up-to-date digital airspace maps besides Airshare?",
 "Flight Advisor", ["The Part 47 register", "The Companies Office", "A real estate site"],
 "AC101-1 says digital, up-to-date maps can be viewed at Flight Advisor, though, like VNCs, they do not show temporary airspace."),
("Where is AIP New Zealand published online?",
 "aip.net.nz", ["airshare.co.nz/aip", "drones.govt.nz", "nzta.govt.nz/aip"],
 "The CAA airspace guide says AIP New Zealand volumes and supplements are available online at www.aip.net.nz."),
("A drone pilot is new to flying. What does the CAA recommend?",
 "Training with an approved provider", ["Learning by trial near airports", "Flying only at night first", "Starting with a 20 kg drone"],
 "AC101-1 recommends training for people new to RPAS, and the CAA keeps a list of approved training organisations at aviation.govt.nz/drone-training."),
("Why does the CAA tell drone pilots to refresh their knowledge of the rules often?",
 "The rules may change", ["Licences expire each month", "Airspace maps are secret", "Rules differ each weekday"],
 "The CAA's brochure says the rules and transport instruments may change over time, so it is good to refresh your knowledge frequently."),
("Which weather condition does AC101-1 list as a hazard for drone flights?",
 "Weather risking loss of control", ["Any cloud in the sky", "Temperatures above 20 degrees", "A sunny afternoon"],
 "AC101-1 Appendix 1 lists flights in inappropriate weather or visibility conditions that could lead to loss of control as potentially hazardous."),
("The CAA says to fly a drone only when what is good?",
 "The visibility", ["The phone signal", "The camera light", "The tide"],
 "The CAA's brochure says to fly only when the visibility is good and to stay clear of fog and cloud, so the drone stays in sight."),
("How does the CAA say an accident or serious incident must first be notified?",
 "By phoning 0508 ACCIDENT", ["By email within 30 days", "By letter to the Minister", "By posting online publicly"],
 "The CAA's guide to reporting says an accident or serious incident must be notified as soon as practicable on 0508 ACCIDENT (0508 222 433)."),
("Where can an aviation occurrence be reported online to the CAA?",
 "aviation.govt.nz/report", ["airshare.co.nz/report", "police.govt.nz/drones", "aip.net.nz/occurrences"],
 "The CAA's reporting guide says occurrences can be reported online at aviation.govt.nz/report, with an email copy sent back."),
("A recreational Part 101 pilot crashes the drone in an empty field, involving no one else. Must it be reported?",
 "No, but it may be reported", ["Yes, within 24 hours", "Yes, to the police", "Yes, to the landowner's insurer"],
 "The CAA's reporting guide says recreational Part 101 operators do not need to report occurrences involving only their own aircraft, though a significant one can still be reported."),
("A drone's battery catches fire in flight. What does the CAA suggest a recreational pilot do?",
 "Report it as a concern", ["Keep it quiet", "Post it only on social media", "Report it to the retailer only"],
 "The CAA's reporting guide says that if an occurrence seems significant to other aviation users, such as a control system failure or a battery fire, it can be reported as an aviation-related concern."),
("How should a Part 102 operator report an occurrence?",
 "As its exposition says", ["Only if someone is hurt", "Only to Airways NZ", "Only once a year"],
 "The CAA's reporting guide says a Part 102 operator who has an occurrence should report it to the CAA as defined in its exposition."),
("When unsure whether to report a drone occurrence, what does the CAA advise?",
 "Err on the side of reporting", ["Wait a month and see", "Ask the drone's retailer", "Report only if it was filmed"],
 "The CAA's guide says if you're unsure whether to report, err on the side of reporting. It strongly encourages reports and will never turn one away."),
("A pilot of a light aircraft has a close call with a drone. How is it reported?",
 "The normal way, as a UAS", ["It cannot be reported", "Only through Airshare", "Only by the drone pilot"],
 "The CAA's reporting guide says an occurrence involving a drone is reported the same way as with any aircraft, identifying the other aircraft as a UAS."),
("Which drone event does the CAA's reporting guide list as typical of one to report?",
 "An airspace incursion", ["A fully charged battery", "A calm sunny flight", "A software update"],
 "The guide's list of typical drone events to report includes injury, loss of control, fly-away, motor or structural failure, incidents with manned aircraft, airspace incursions and third-party damage."),
]
